# Netlify serves every first-party asset as `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# by default, because the filenames are not fingerprinted. ETags mean repeat
# visitors get 304s rather than re-downloads, so the cost is a conditional
# round trip per asset per visit — about ten of them, which is noticeable on
# mobile.
#
# NOTE ON `immutable`: only content-addressed filenames get a long TTL.
#
# /vendor/ is effectively immutable — every file carries its exact upstream
# version in the name (react-18.3.1..., leaflet-1.9.4...) and a version bump
# changes the filename — so it gets the full year.
#
# assets/pages.<hash>.css carries a content hash, so it gets the year too.
# Editing it produces a new filename and a new URL; nothing can go stale.
#
# Everything else under /assets/ is NOT hashed (logo.webp, douro-*.webp,
# og-image.jpg). Those had one week, and that was a mistake we shipped: when
# pages.css was unhashed, every visitor who had loaded the site was pinned to
# a stale stylesheet for up to a week, and the header rendered unstyled. One
# day bounds that damage while still covering repeat visits. Hash the filename
# of anything under here that changes with the markup.
#
# HTML stays uncached so content and CMS-driven markup update immediately.
# Netlify already sets HSTS.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Content-hashed CSS, in its own directory for two reasons: Netlify's _headers
# matches a trailing splat and not a wildcard inside a filename (so an earlier
# /assets/pages.*.css rule silently never matched), and where two rules both
# match a path the LATER one wins — so this must sit after /assets/* to
# override it. Both were verified against production rather than assumed.
/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
